WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.470
Imagine a household gets a pay rise:

2
00:00:02.470 --> 00:00:05.700
from 500 to 520 a week.

3
00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:06.930
They buy more clothes.

4
00:00:06.930 --> 00:00:08.780
They eat out more often.

5
00:00:08.780 --> 00:00:11.360
But the instant noodles
in their weekly shop drop

6
00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:13.980
from 20 packs to 18.

7
00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:16.900
More money, yet less of something.

8
00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:20.990
When people get richer, why do
they buy less of some things?

9
00:00:20.990 --> 00:00:23.970
In this mission, you'll
slide incomes up and down

10
00:00:23.970 --> 00:00:27.420
and watch the demand curves
for different goods respond.

11
00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:30.400
Then you'll turn each
change into one number,

12
00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:34.390
income elasticity, and
read its sign and size.

13
00:00:34.390 --> 00:00:38.690
Your mission: find out why more
income can mean less demand.
